1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:35,280
We're detecting a high energy reaction
from inside the target!

37
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,200
What?!

38
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,620
The circumference area is accelerating!
It's converging!

39
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:39,280
It can't be!

40
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:47,170
No, dodge it!

41
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:57,220
Retrieve him, hurry!

42
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:05,020
The target has gone silent!

43
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:06,100
How's Shinji?

44
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:06,930
He's alive!

45
00:02:06,930 --> 00:02:10,310
Unit 01 has been recovered.
En route to the 7th cage.

46
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:12,400
I'm going to the cage.
Take over for me, please!

47
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:16,820
Unit 01 secured!

48
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:17,400
Hurry with the cooling!

49
00:02:18,450 --> 00:02:21,070
The pilot's brain waves are erratic!

50
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,330
His pulse is very weak.

51
00:02:22,330 --> 00:02:25,750
Increase life support to maximum power.
Give him a heart massage.

52
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:26,160
Yes, Ma'am!

53
00:02:27,330 --> 00:02:28,830
Pulse confirmed!

54
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:30,880
Force eject the entry plug! Hurry!

55
00:02:34,550 --> 00:02:36,420
Emergency LCL discharge!

56
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:37,090
Yes, Ma'am!

57
00:02:38,130 --> 00:02:40,340
Come on, open the hatch! Hurry!

58
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:51,100
Shinji!

59
00:03:17,130 --> 00:03:20,590
EPISODE SIX
DECISIVE BATTLE,
NEW TOKYO-3

60
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:27,890
1/1 Scale Balloon Dummy

61
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:36,360
The enemy's particle beam cannon has hit!

62
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,900
The dummy has been vaporized!

63
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:38,610
Next.

64
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:44,910
Automated Model 12 Self-Propelled Mortar

65
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:54,710
The Model 12 Self-Propelled Mortar
has been destroyed!

66
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:57,170
I see.

67
00:03:58,130 --> 00:04:02,300
From the data we've collected,
we're assuming that the target

68
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:05,430
automatically attacks any opponent
within a certain range.

69
00:04:05,430 --> 00:04:10,140
The likelihood of it hitting anything entering
the area with its particle beam is 100%.

70
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:08,930
Department of Operations, Nerv Headquarters
Analysis Room 2

71
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:13,730
It's too risky for close range combat
in an Eva, isn't it?

72
00:04:13,730 --> 00:04:15,350
What about its AT field?

73
00:04:15,350 --> 00:04:16,440
It's still active.

74
00:04:15,350 --> 00:04:22,030
REPLAY IMAGE

75
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:20,780
It's strong enough that the spatial changes
in phase are visible to the naked eye.

76
00:04:22,030 --> 00:04:25,740
Using half-measures like guided missiles,
artillery, or bombs

77
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:28,030
will inflict more damage on us
than on the Angel!

78
00:04:28,030 --> 00:04:32,830
Offensively and defensively it's
almost perfect. A flying fortress.

79
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:34,920
What's the status on its drill?

80
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:37,290
At this moment the target
is directly above us,

81
00:04:37,290 --> 00:04:40,130
penetrating the New Tokyo-3 Null Zone.

82
00:04:40,130 --> 00:04:43,170
A giant shielded drill with
a diameter of 17.5 meters

83
00:04:43,170 --> 00:04:46,050
is boring towards Nerv HQ.

84
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:51,680
The enemy is planning to attack Nerv
Headquarters directly.

85
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,560
Sassy bastard!

86
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,020
So, what's its ETA?

87
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:59,940
Japan Standard Time
Remaining Estimated Time

88
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:59,940
12:06:54 AM.

89
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:03,570
By that time, it will have breached
all twenty-two levels of armor,

90
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:06,860
APPROXIMATED
GRAPHICS

91
00:05:03,570 --> 00:05:06,030
and arrive at Nerv Headquarters itself.

92
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:09,450
Less than ten hours...

93
00:05:14,410 --> 00:05:17,580
PRESENT TIME

94
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:17,580
The drill has contacted the first armor plate.

95
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:20,380
What's the condition of Unit 01?

96
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:24,170
The defensive armor was melted
down to the third layer.

97
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:23,380
Cage 7, Nerv Headquarters

98
00:05:24,170 --> 00:05:28,300
The silver lining is that the central
control unit sustained no damage.

99
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:31,720
Three more seconds, and
it would have been over.

100
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:35,390
In three hours, the replacement parts
should be installed.

101
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:36,730
Roger.

102
00:05:36,730 --> 00:05:38,020
What's the status of Unit 00?

103
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,480
Re-activation itself should
prove no problem,

104
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:43,110
but there's still a feedback error.

105
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:44,150
So actual combat...

106
00:05:44,150 --> 00:05:46,360
...is still impossible.

107
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:49,030
What's the condition of Unit 01's pilot?

108
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:51,990
Emergency Room, Central Hospital,
Nerv Headquarters

109
00:05:49,030 --> 00:05:50,780
No physical damage.

110
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:54,000
However, his nerve pulses are up by 0.8.

111
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,250
Still within acceptable limits.

112
00:05:56,250 --> 00:06:00,420
Enemy drill arrival: 9 hours, 55 minutes.

113
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:02,670
The situation certainly isn't favorable.

114
00:06:02,670 --> 00:06:04,840
Shall we just raise a white flag?

115
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:05,970
Before we resort to that,

116
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:08,590
there's one little thing I'd like to try.

117
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:14,020
You want a sniper to shoot the target
from outside its firing zone?

118
00:06:14,010 --> 00:06:17,520
Nerv Commander's Office

119
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:15,060
Yes, Sir.

120
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:17,440
Instead of trying to neutralize
the target's AT field,

121
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:21,190
I believe a pinpoint shot with a
high-energy beam is the only way.

122
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,730
What do the Magi say?

123
00:06:22,730 --> 00:06:25,150
The responses from the Magi
Super Computers

124
00:06:25,150 --> 00:06:28,610
were two affirmative and
one conditional affirmative.

125
00:06:28,610 --> 00:06:31,780
So, our probability of success is 8.7 percent.

126
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:34,080
It's quite a high percentage.

127
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:38,790
I see no reason to raise an objection.
You may proceed, Captain Katsuragi.

128
00:06:38,790 --> 00:06:40,540
Yes, Sir.

129
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:43,710
But you sure have come up with
a reckless plan,

130
00:06:43,710 --> 00:06:45,630
Operations Director Katsuragi.

131
00:06:45,630 --> 00:06:47,880
Don't be rude. It's not reckless!

132
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:50,300
It can be executed within the
nine hours we have left,

133
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:52,600
and has the highest chance of success.

134
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,140
This thing does? Really?

135
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:58,640
Eva Positron Rifle
(Prototype 20 with Toroidal Accelerator)

136
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:59,100
But our positron rifle can't handle
such a high output.

137
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,060
What are you going to do about that?

138
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:02,940
We'll borrow one, of course.

139
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:06,030
Borrow one? You don't mean...

140
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:09,320
Right! The Strategic SDF Lab's prototype!

141
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,070
Requisition Order

142
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:15,790
Nerv is hereby requisitioning this
Self Propelled Positron Cannon

143
00:07:15,790 --> 00:07:18,410
as of 15:00 today.

144
00:07:18,370 --> 00:07:21,870
Tsukuba Technology Laboratory Headquarters, Strategic SDF

145
00:07:18,410 --> 00:07:21,870
But still, this is ridiculous!

146
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:24,840
Special Units Hangar 4

147
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:26,840
We'll try to return this in as close
to its original condition as we can.

148
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:30,220
We appreciate your cooperation!

149
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:32,890
Okay, Rei! Take it away!

150
00:07:36,010 --> 00:07:38,850
That's a piece of precision machinery,
so be careful!

151
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:45,820
Even so, our calculations
show that it will take

152
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:48,650
at least 180 million kilowatts to
penetrate that AT field.

153
00:07:48,650 --> 00:07:51,950
Where are you going to get
that much electricity?

154
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:55,830
Where else? From all of Japan!

155
00:07:57,740 --> 00:08:01,660
Giant Power Outage Today All Across Japan

156
00:07:57,950 --> 00:07:59,870
We apologize for interrupting

157
00:07:59,870 --> 00:08:02,920
our regular programming for this
Emergency Bulletin.

158
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:03,580
Suzuhara Residence

159
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:05,710
From 11:30 PM tonight
until tomorrow morning,

160
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:05,330
Horaki Residence

161
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:07,840
New Tokyo-2

162
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:08,590
there will be a large scale power blackout

163
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:09,960
throughout most of Japan.

164
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:11,340
New Makurazaki, Kagoshima Prefecture

165
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:13,050
We appreciate your cooperation.

166
00:08:13,050 --> 00:08:19,220
Repeat, from 11:30 PM tonight
until tomorrow morning

167
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:17,810
At dawn today,
a large-scale
 power outage
all across the nation.

168
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:15,720
Betsukai, Hokkaido

169
00:08:17,810 --> 00:08:20,520
Ube, Yamaguchi Prefecture

170
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:21,810
there will be a large scale power
blackout throughout Japan.

171
00:08:21,810 --> 00:08:24,850
We appreciate your cooperation.

172
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:25,270
Mitaka Ward, Old Tokyo

173
00:08:26,770 --> 00:08:28,770
New Tokyo-3

174
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:31,940
Control Room, General Operations
Command Center, Nerv Headquarters

175
00:08:29,150 --> 00:08:32,110
The drill has just broken through
the seventh defensive layer.

176
00:08:32,110 --> 00:08:33,860
What's the status on our energy system?

177
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:36,370
New Odawara, Kanagawa Prefecture

178
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:40,200
3.2% behind schedule, but we should
manage to be finished by 23:10.

179
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,790
And the positron rifle?

180
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:44,580
On the honor of Technology
Development Department 3,

181
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:45,790
Technology Department Division 3, Nerv Headquarters
(In charge of electromagnetic and light wave hardware)

182
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:47,590
we'll have it built for you in three hours.

183
00:08:47,590 --> 00:08:48,710
What about our defensive measures?

184
00:08:48,710 --> 00:08:52,210
Well, using a shield is about all we can do.

185
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:51,460
Hangar 8, Nerv Headquarters

186
00:08:51,550 --> 00:08:55,590
Eva Anti-Heat and Light Wave Defensive Equipment
(Makeshift Specs)

187
00:08:52,210 --> 00:08:54,260
So, this is the shield?

188
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:57,600
Yes. It's a hand-me-down from
a single stage to orbit rocket.

189
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:03,060
It may look ugly, but it's got a super-
electromagnetic base coating that

190
00:09:03,060 --> 00:09:06,100
Section 2 guarantees will stand up to
the enemy's particle beam

191
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,520
for at least seventeen seconds.

192
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:10,360
Good. Have you determined
the sniper position?

193
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,490
Given the range to the target,
geographical features,

194
00:09:12,490 --> 00:09:16,110
and taking power access into consideration,
this would be the spot.

195
00:09:16,110 --> 00:09:19,330
Definitely looks good.

196
00:09:19,330 --> 00:09:21,740
The sniping position will be atop Mt. Futago!

197
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:24,960
The operation will commence
at 00:00 tomorrow morning!

198
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:28,080
From this point on, this operation will be
called "Operation Yashima".

199
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,500
Roger.

200
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:31,630
Now, the only remaining problem
is the pilot.

201
00:09:45,730 --> 00:09:48,150
Unit 01's designated pilot is conscious now.

202
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:49,770
Cage 7 Control Room

203
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:50,360
His examination results look normal.

204
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:54,320
Good. Then, the operation will
proceed as planned.

205
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,490
Roger.

206
00:09:55,490 --> 00:09:57,740
But I wonder if he'll pilot it again.

207
00:09:58,610 --> 00:10:00,660
Get ready for a decisive battle at Mt. Futago!

208
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:04,160
Surgical Ward 3, Central Hospital

209
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:20,220
Ayanami...

210
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:22,720
I'm here to brief you on the timetable
of Operation Yashima,

211
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:25,390
which will begin tomorrow at 00:00 hours.

212
00:10:26,890 --> 00:10:32,940
Pilots Ikari and Ayanami will arrive
at the cage at 17:30 today.

213
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:37,240
At 18:00, Units 01 and 00 will activate.

214
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,530
Launch is at 18:05.

215
00:10:39,530 --> 00:10:42,830
They will arrive at the temporary base
on Mt. Futago at 18:30.

216
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:45,540
There, they will stand by and
await further orders.

217
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:49,250
The operation will begin
promptly at midnight.

218
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,330
Here's a new one.

219
00:10:58,970 --> 00:11:01,680
Don't show up half-asleep looking like that.

220
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:09,560
Sorry.

221
00:11:13,730 --> 00:11:16,570
All I've been doing since
yesterday is apologizing.

222
00:11:18,150 --> 00:11:19,650
Your meal.

223
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:26,080
I don't want to eat anything.

224
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:28,750
We'll be departing in sixty minutes.

225
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:32,330
Do I have to pilot that thing again?

226
00:11:32,330 --> 00:11:33,830
Yes, you do.

227
00:11:34,630 --> 00:11:37,340
I don't want to.

228
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,880
Maybe you can be so cool about it,

229
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:41,760
because you haven't had the kind
of experiences I've had yet.

230
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:45,640
I don't want to go through that again.

231
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:46,850
Then why don't you stay in bed?

232
00:11:47,970 --> 00:11:49,350
Stay in bed?

233
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:52,480
I'll pilot Unit 01.

234
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:58,900
Dr. Akagi is already prepared to rewrite
Unit 01's personal data files.

235
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:00,780
Miss Ritsuko is...

236
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:04,990
I'm leaving. Captain Katsuragi and
Dr. Akagi will be waiting at the cage.

237
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:10,290
Goodbye.

238
00:12:26,010 --> 00:12:28,010
No School Today

239
00:12:26,010 --> 00:12:28,010
New Tokyo-3 Public Middle School 1 Principal

240
00:12:28,010 --> 00:12:32,640
They're awfully late. We oughta
evacuate to the shelter.

241
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:35,310
I hacked into my dad's data files.

242
00:12:35,310 --> 00:12:37,440
I'm sure this is the time.

243
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:39,650
Yeah, but they still ain't here.

244
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:47,030
The mountain is moving.

245
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:48,330
The Evangelions!

246
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,090
Cool!

247
00:13:00,090 --> 00:13:07,720
Go for it! We're counting on you!
Evangelion! Good luck!

248
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:10,260
8:11 PM

249
00:13:12,890 --> 00:13:16,600
Near Asahi Falls on Mt. Futago

250
00:13:13,230 --> 00:13:16,100
The drill has penetrated through
the 17th layer of armor.

251
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:19,150
It will reach headquarters in
3 hours 55 minutes.

252
00:13:19,150 --> 00:13:21,190
No problem with the hub
synchronization system.

253
00:13:21,190 --> 00:13:24,360
Power supply transfer from Shikoku
and Kyushu is completed.

254
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:27,160
Begin tests of each cooling system.

255
00:13:27,870 --> 00:13:30,700
This is a piece of precision machinery,
so handle it carefully.

256
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:38,540
Eva Positron Sniper Rifle
(Nerv Specs - Formerly Strategic SDF Lab's Automated Positron Rifle)

257
00:13:32,330 --> 00:13:36,710
This thing wasn't built for field operations.
Will it really work?

258
00:13:36,710 --> 00:13:39,960
There's no choice.
This is a makeshift solution.

259
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,460
So it'll be okay?

260
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:43,010
Theoretically, yes.

261
00:13:43,010 --> 00:13:47,800
However, we won't know if the cannon barrel
and accelerator will hold until we try firing it.

262
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:50,930
This is the first time it's been fired
with such a high power output.

263
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:56,480
Here are your individual duties
for the operation.

264
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,230
Shinji...

265
00:13:56,980 --> 00:13:58,020
Yes, Ma'am.

266
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,860
Your Unit 01 will be the gunner.

267
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:00,900
Yes, Ma'am.

268
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:03,320
Rei, you're in charge of defense with Unit 00.

269
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:04,440
Yes, Ma'am.

270
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:08,740
This is because Shinji has a higher
sync ratio with Unit 01,

271
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:12,410
and this operation will require
exceptional precision.

272
00:14:12,410 --> 00:14:14,240
Since the positron beam will be
influenced by the Earth's gravity,

273
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:17,920
magnetic fields and rotation,
it will not fire in a straight line.

274
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:21,170
You must remember to make
adjustments for these deviations.

275
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:24,250
You must penetrate the core precisely.

276
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:28,260
But I've never practiced this!

277
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:29,640
Don't worry.

278
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,680
Just do what the manual says.

279
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:35,720
When the indicators converge
in the center, pull the trigger.

280
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:38,230
The computers will handle the rest.

281
00:14:38,230 --> 00:14:40,230
Also, once you fire it,

282
00:14:40,230 --> 00:14:42,440
it will take time before you can fire again

283
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:45,400
for cooling, reloading,
and replacement of the fuses.

284
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:48,610
Then, if I miss and the enemy shoots back...

285
00:14:48,610 --> 00:14:50,820
Don't think about unnecessary
things right now.

286
00:14:50,820 --> 00:14:53,530
Just think about destroying it in one shot.

287
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:58,160
So it's crisis time.

288
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:00,420
I...

289
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:02,790
I just need to defend Unit 01, correct?

290
00:15:02,790 --> 00:15:04,340
That's right.

291
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:06,130
Understood.

292
00:15:06,130 --> 00:15:09,220
It's time. Both of you, get changed.

293
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,180
Yes, Ma'am.

294
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:23,860
We might die doing this.

295
00:15:25,270 --> 00:15:27,150
Why do you say that?

296
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,820
You won't die.

297
00:15:34,530 --> 00:15:36,240
Because I'll protect you.

298
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,040
...a large-scale power outage all across...

299
00:16:17,450 --> 00:16:20,250
Why do you pilot this thing?

300
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:25,960
Because I'm bound.

301
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:26,880
Bound?

302
00:16:28,090 --> 00:16:30,300
Yes, it's a bond.

303
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,880
With my father?

304
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,140
With all people.

305
00:16:36,090 --> 00:16:39,890
You're very strong, Ayanami.

306
00:16:39,890 --> 00:16:43,850
Because I have nothing else.

307
00:16:43,850 --> 00:16:45,810
What do you mean, "you have nothing else"?

308
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:50,150
It's time. Let's go.

309
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:53,570
Goodbye.

310
00:17:05,830 --> 00:17:10,800
The time is now 00:00:00.

311
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,960
Type 14 Large Mobile Command Car

312
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:13,920
Japan Standard Time

313
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:16,930
Commencing operation.

314
00:17:14,930 --> 00:17:16,050
Inside Command Car

315
00:17:16,930 --> 00:17:21,140
Shinji, we're entrusting you with
all the electricity of Japan.

316
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:22,100
Good luck.

317
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:23,180
Yes, Ma'am!

318
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:25,390
Initiate primary connection.

319
00:17:25,390 --> 00:17:28,440
Initiating power transmission from
districts number 1 through 803.

320
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,650
Number 1 transmission system nominal.

321
00:17:33,490 --> 00:17:35,740
No problem with hub synchronizer output.

322
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:37,860
All transmission induction systems activated.

323
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:39,370
Conversion efficiency staying
within estimated values.

324
00:17:38,490 --> 00:17:40,740
Voltage is rising. Reaching pressure zone.

325
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:43,370
All cooling systems, full power!

326
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:47,170
Electron condenser system nominal.

327
00:17:46,330 --> 00:17:48,250
Auxiliary system activated.

328
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,330
Temperature stable. No problems detected.

329
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:52,460
Positron charge is nominal.

330
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:53,880
Initiate secondary connection!

331
00:17:55,090 --> 00:17:57,380
All accelerators engaging.

332
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:59,300
Activate convergence unit.

333
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:02,560
Transmitting all power to Mt. Futago
temporary substation.

334
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:05,140
No problems reported
with tertiary connection.

335
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:07,520
Release final safety systems.

336
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:08,560
Clear the chamber!

337
00:18:09,810 --> 00:18:09,980
Safe Empty

338
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:10,560
Armed
Loaded

339
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:16,450
Error correction for Earth rotation
and gravity is plus 0.0009.

340
00:18:16,450 --> 00:18:19,490
Voltage is 0.2 short of critical.

341
00:18:26,370 --> 00:18:27,660
Seventh and final connection engaged!

342
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:29,710
All photo-electron fuses,
commence convergence!

343
00:18:29,710 --> 00:18:32,040
Transmitting all energy to the positron rifle!

344
00:18:33,130 --> 00:18:34,090
8...

345
00:18:34,090 --> 00:18:35,130
7...

346
00:18:35,130 --> 00:18:36,130
6...

347
00:18:36,130 --> 00:18:37,050
5...

348
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:38,340
High energy output detected from the target!

349
00:18:37,050 --> 00:18:38,050
4...

350
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:39,260
3...

351
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:39,260
What did you say?

352
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:40,180
2...

353
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:41,470
1...

354
00:18:41,470 --> 00:18:42,300
Fire!

355
00:19:01,910 --> 00:19:02,740
We missed?

356
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:15,170
The enemy drill has broken
into the Geo-Front!

357
00:19:15,170 --> 00:19:16,710
Fire two! Hurry!

358
00:19:17,710 --> 00:19:20,050
Replacing fuses! Initiating recharge!

359
00:19:20,050 --> 00:19:21,390
Barrel cooling in progress!

360
00:19:21,390 --> 00:19:23,140
Resume positron acceleration!

361
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:26,220
Another high energy reading
coming from the target!

362
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:27,220
Oh, no!

363
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:30,640
Shinji!

364
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,780
Ayanami!

365
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,120
The shield won't last!

366
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:44,030
Aren't we ready yet?!

367
00:19:44,030 --> 00:19:45,120
Ten more seconds!

368
00:19:46,370 --> 00:19:48,040
Hurry up!

369
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:51,750
Hurry up!

370
00:19:58,300 --> 00:19:59,460
Yes!

371
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:06,430
Ayanami!

372
00:20:37,290 --> 00:20:38,800
Ayanami!

373
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:40,510
Are you all right?!

374
00:20:40,510 --> 00:20:42,050
Ayanami!

375
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:58,110
Don't say... Don't say that
you have nothing else.

376
00:21:00,780 --> 00:21:04,910
Don't say goodbye when you leave
on a mission. It's too sad.

377
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:23,510
Why are you crying?

378
00:21:27,470 --> 00:21:32,560
I'm sorry. I don't know what to do
at a time like this.

379
00:21:34,390 --> 00:21:36,230
You can just smile.

380
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:00,460
TO BE CONTINUED

381
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:06,780
PREVIEW

382
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:09,740
The humanoid weapon
that the civilans developed

383
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:12,320
to fight against the encroaching Angels
goes out of control.

384
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:15,410
Will Misato be able to stop the meltdown?

385
00:23:15,410 --> 00:23:17,790
It's the next episode:
"That Which is Manmade"

386
00:23:17,790 --> 00:23:19,000
Look forward to it!

387
00:23:18,790 --> 00:23:20,920
THAT WHICH IS MANMADE
